WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.282
Open WebUI becomes useful when it is connected to model backends.

00:00:04.282 --> 00:00:07.704
Those backends may be local inference services, remote APIs,

00:00:07.704 --> 00:00:10.365
or OpenAI-compatible endpoints at a high level.

00:00:10.365 --> 00:00:14.547
The connection usually depends on an endpoint address, supported API shape,

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:17.208
authentication details, available model names, network reachability,

00:00:17.208 --> 00:00:20.630
and settings such as context length or generation parameters.

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:23.671
Model selection should be tied to use case.

00:00:23.671 --> 00:00:28.613
A lightweight local model may be fine for casual drafting, while document analysis,

00:00:28.613 --> 00:00:32.415
code help, or structured extraction may need a different model.

00:00:32.415 --> 00:00:36.597
Temperature and sampling settings influence how deterministic or varied responses feel.

00:00:36.597 --> 00:00:41.159
Context length affects how much conversation and supporting material can be considered,

00:00:41.159 --> 00:00:44.581
but larger context can increase resource use and latency.

00:00:44.581 --> 00:00:47.242
Connectivity testing should be basic and repeatable.

00:00:47.242 --> 00:00:51.424
Confirm that the endpoint is reachable from the Open WebUI host,

00:00:51.424 --> 00:00:54.845
that credentials are valid, that the expected models appear,

00:00:54.845 --> 00:00:57.887
and that a simple prompt returns a response.

00:00:57.887 --> 00:01:02.449
Failed connections may come from network binding, firewall rules, incorrect base URLs,

00:01:02.449 --> 00:01:06.251
unavailable runtimes, invalid keys, missing models, or incompatible API behavior.

00:01:06.251 --> 00:01:08.152
Document approved models and endpoints.

00:01:08.152 --> 00:01:13.474
Operators should know which endpoints are local, which are remote, which use private data,

00:01:13.474 --> 00:01:17.276
which are experimental, and which are appropriate for specific workflows.

00:01:17.276 --> 00:01:21.458
Documentation reduces confusion when models are renamed, moved, upgraded, or retired.

00:01:21.458 --> 00:01:26.020
It also helps users avoid sending sensitive work to the wrong backend.
